 ## Overview
-Volume Material Setup initializes the rendering state for direct volume ray casting by creating and caching a material object configured for transparent volumetric rendering [S1, S2, unofficial]. It binds necessary textures (noise, fire profiles, transfer functions, labels, weights) and uniform parameters (affine transforms, intensity ranges) to the GPU, enabling the shader to correctly sample and composite volume data [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods by focusing on the binding and configuration of material resources rather than the traversal logic or the transfer function definition itself [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Volume Material Setup initializes the rendering state for direct volume ray casting by creating and caching a `RawShaderMaterial` configured for transparent volumetric rendering [S2, unofficial]. It binds necessary textures (noise, fire profiles, transfer functions, labels, weights) and uniform parameters (affine transforms, intensity ranges) to the GPU, enabling the shader to correctly sample and composite volume data [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods by focusing exclusively on the binding and configuration of material resources rather than the traversal logic or transfer function definition itself [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method constructs a material object that encapsulates all shader inputs required for volume rendering [S1, S2, unofficial]. It handles the selection of textures based on availability, computes inverse affine matrices for coordinate transformation, and sets flags to inform the shader about the data type (e.g., label map vs. continuous) [S1, unofficial].
+The method constructs a material object that encapsulates all shader inputs required for volume rendering [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It handles the selection of textures based on availability, computes inverse affine matrices for coordinate transformation, and sets flags to inform the shader about the data type (e.g., label map vs. continuous) [S1, unofficial].
 
